# Copy to `.env` in this directory for optional compose variables (e.g. published ports).
#
# PostgreSQL credentials are not passed through compose environment variables. Use the Docker
# secret file `.gc_docker_secrets/ground_control_postgres_password` (Launcher → Settings → Docker
# secrets, or edit the file). If you previously used `GC_POSTGRES_PASSWORD` in `.env`, the
# launcher copies it into that secret file once when the secret is still empty.
# If you had no `.env` and only relied on an older compose file, put the same password you used
# when the Postgres volume was first created into that secret file before starting containers.
#
# Optional: compose sets GROUND_CONTROL_DOCKER_EGRESS_HOST=host.docker.internal so firewall
# inventory using 127.0.0.1 or localhost reaches the Docker host from inside the container.
# LAN IP firewalls need normal L2/L3 routing from the container (no extra GC setting).
